You are requested to write a serverless function for the following requirement:
           Task Summary: This task automates LinkedIn's hiring flow.  It integrates with the LinkedIn API to extract applicant data (Name, Profile URL, Email, Job Title, etc.) and saves it to an Excel sheet.  It also automates email responses with customizable templates and confirmation prompts before sending each email.  Requires LinkedIn API keys, email service credentials, desired Excel sheet columns, and email template content.
           Function Details:
           - Name: fetchLinkedInApplicants
           - Description: Fetches new applicants from LinkedIn API and stores them in the database
           Endpoint Details:
           - Path: /api/fetch-applicants
           - Method: GET

           The following packages are installed in the project:
           - @microfox/null
- @microfox/aws-ses
- @microfox/google-sdk
           - @prisma/client
           - dotenv

           Requirements:
           - Use TypeScript
           - Implement proper error handling
           - Use Prisma client (import prisma from '../db/prisma') for database operations
           - Follow Serverless best practices
           - Add proper Docs
           - Add appropriate comments
           - Return properly formatted responses

           Complete example for a function stored at src/functions/getExternalData.ts:
           import prisma from '../db/prisma'

/**
* GET endpoint to fetch data from an external API
*/
export const getExternalData = async (event: any) => {
try {
  // Example: Fetching data from a public API
  const response = await fetch('https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/1')
  const data = await response.json()
  return {
    statusCode: 200,
    body: JSON.stringify(data),
  }
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Error fetching external data:', error)
  return {
    statusCode: 500,
    body: JSON.stringify({ error: error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unknown error' }),
  }
} finally {
  await prisma.$disconnect()
}
}

/**
* Documentation for external API endpoints
*/
export const getExternalDataDocs = {
title: 'Get External Data',
description: 'Retrieve data from an external API',
method: 'GET',
path: '/external',
responses: {
  200: {
    description: 'External data retrieved successfully',
    schema: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        userId: { type: 'number' },
        id: { type: 'number' },
        title: { type: 'string' },
        body: { type: 'string' },
      },
    },
  },
  500: {
    description: 'Server error',
    schema: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: {
        error: { type: 'string' },
      },
    },
  },
},
}

           The code should be created in the src/functions directory.
           Make sure to use the prisma client for database operations.
           Make sure to use the necessary imports from the packages when needed.
           Use named exports for the function.
           Also export the doc file for the function.
           Only use the packages that are listed above in the project.
           Make no assumption of utils, or outside files - Create complete functionality in a single file.
           Do not write any mock code, it should be production ready code.

